--
libstdc++ 13 <format>: std::format("{}", 42) is empty.  Fixed (round
163w): format:1422 __formatter_fp::format was instantiated for int, because
formatter<int, char> selected the floating-point partial specialization
(cpp20_partial_specialization_type_constraint), and _M_format_arg's
visitor lambda, which uses `this', got a closure
(cpp14_lambda_this_capture_member_calls).  _M_parse_format_spec was
dropped because formatter<int, char> was the primary template (int and
wchar_t were one type, cpp11_specialization_distinguishes_fundamental_
types).  Still dropped: format:3124 basic_format_arg::_M_visit, `format'
and two closure `operator()'s; conversion and verification now take more
than 25 minutes.  g++ 13 accepts this program, and it fails only its
WRONG assertion.
